\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {section}{\numberline {1}Introduction}{1}{section.1}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {The paper in one figure: the statistic moves, admission does not, suppression does not follow.} \textbf  {(a)} Two paths run from an upstream rescaling $T$ to suppression: the \emph  {chain} a preservation criterion reasons along, and a \emph  {confounded} path on which $T$ merely attenuates whichever client carries the poison (Lem.~\ref {lem:annihilation}) and reaches ASR \textbf  {without passing through $d_2$'s statistic at all}. \textbf  {Mode~S cuts the second by construction}, pinning every adversary at $c{=}1$ (\textbf  {the one channel the dose closes, and not the only thing it moves}), which is what makes the chain's two broken arrows measurable. The admission count pools the four aggregators of Table~\ref {tab:channels}, with adversarial mass present at baseline in $100$ of those $240$ rounds; Krum alone admits no adversary at any rung, so its own zero is a floor. \textbf  {But the non-event is not only a Krum floor effect}: reputation and \texttt  {coord\_median} each admit adversarial mass at baseline in $48$ of their $60$ measured rounds, and the support of that mass still never moves (App.~\ref {app:channel_table}). \textbf  {(b)} Mode~S, Krum under model-scaling (§\ref {sec:targeted}): as $\rho $ grows to $54.6$ the \emph  {decision} flips in up to $80\%$ of rounds while the \emph  {support} of the admitted adversarial mass does not, and max-committed ASR stays inside the pre-specified $\pm 0.15$ equivalence margin ($|\Delta |{=}0.026$). Bars are Student-$t$ $95\%$ intervals ($n{=}5$), recomputed per seed.}}{2}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:modeS}{{1}{2}{\textbf {The paper in one figure: the statistic moves, admission does not, suppression does not follow.} \textbf {(a)} Two paths run from an upstream rescaling $T$ to suppression: the \emph {chain} a preservation criterion reasons along, and a \emph {confounded} path on which $T$ merely attenuates whichever client carries the poison (Lem.~\ref {lem:annihilation}) and reaches ASR \textbf {without passing through $d_2$'s statistic at all}. \textbf {Mode~S cuts the second by construction}, pinning every adversary at $c{=}1$ (\textbf {the one channel the dose closes, and not the only thing it moves}), which is what makes the chain's two broken arrows measurable. The admission count pools the four aggregators of Table~\ref {tab:channels}, with adversarial mass present at baseline in $100$ of those $240$ rounds; Krum alone admits no adversary at any rung, so its own zero is a floor. \textbf {But the non-event is not only a Krum floor effect}: reputation and \texttt {coord\_median} each admit adversarial mass at baseline in $48$ of their $60$ measured rounds, and the support of that mass still never moves (App.~\ref {app:channel_table}). \textbf {(b)} Mode~S, Krum under model-scaling (§\ref {sec:targeted}): as $\rho $ grows to $54.6$ the \emph {decision} flips in up to $80\%$ of rounds while the \emph {support} of the admitted adversarial mass does not, and max-committed ASR stays inside the pre-specified $\pm 0.15$ equivalence margin ($|\Delta |{=}0.026$). Bars are Student-$t$ $95\%$ intervals ($n{=}5$), recomputed per seed}{figure.caption.1}{}}
