\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {The four channels, all four aggregators, under Mode~S}; endpoint change $\kappa {=}0 \to \kappa {=}2$. \textbf  {$\Delta $~agg.\ is the relative displacement of the aggregate the defense \emph  {emits}}, $\|\mathrm  {agg}(T(U)) - \mathrm  {agg}(U)\|/\|\mathrm  {agg}(U)\|$, so it is what enters training and \textbf  {not} the value of a scoring statistic. \textbf  {$\Delta $~adm.\ is the \emph  {support} of the admitted adversarial mass and $\Delta \Lambda _a$ is the separate influence question}, the weight the adversary's direction carries; the two are never interchangeable. The decision/admission dissociation is not one aggregator's property: it holds for a selector, a cosine-invariant selector, a coordinate-wise order statistic and a weighted averager. The table does \textbf  {not} order the arms, $\Delta \Lambda _a$ and $\Delta $ASR disagreeing in rank, which is this section's refutation stated in one row-pair, and it is \emph  {not} an out-of-sample test. Row~5 replicates row~1 on a second dataset and architecture with its channels measured \emph  {before} its ASR existed; row~6 is the pre-registered score-only control, row~1 with the magnitude channel closed, so its decision, admission and influence columns are row~1's own. Every cell is emitted from frozen artifacts by a single generator (App.~\ref {app:channel_table}).}}{6}{table.caption.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:channels}{{1}{6}{\textbf {The four channels, all four aggregators, under Mode~S}; endpoint change $\kappa {=}0 \to \kappa {=}2$. \textbf {$\Delta $~agg.\ is the relative displacement of the aggregate the defense \emph {emits}}, $\|\mathrm {agg}(T(U)) - \mathrm {agg}(U)\|/\|\mathrm {agg}(U)\|$, so it is what enters training and \textbf {not} the value of a scoring statistic. \textbf {$\Delta $~adm.\ is the \emph {support} of the admitted adversarial mass and $\Delta \Lambda _a$ is the separate influence question}, the weight the adversary's direction carries; the two are never interchangeable. The decision/admission dissociation is not one aggregator's property: it holds for a selector, a cosine-invariant selector, a coordinate-wise order statistic and a weighted averager. The table does \textbf {not} order the arms, $\Delta \Lambda _a$ and $\Delta $ASR disagreeing in rank, which is this section's refutation stated in one row-pair, and it is \emph {not} an out-of-sample test. Row~5 replicates row~1 on a second dataset and architecture with its channels measured \emph {before} its ASR existed; row~6 is the pre-registered score-only control, row~1 with the magnitude channel closed, so its decision, admission and influence columns are row~1's own. Every cell is emitted from frozen artifacts by a single generator (App.~\ref {app:channel_table})}{table.caption.6}{}}
